{
  "kanda": "kishkindha",
  "sarga": 62,
  "title": "Sampaati's legend [contd.]",
  "sourceUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/kish/sarga62/kishkindhasans62.htm",
  "romanUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/kish/sarga62/kishkindhaitrans62.htm",
  "translator": "Desiraju Hanumanta Rao",
  "introduction": [
    "Sage Nishaakara asks Sampaati to wait for monkeys who arrive at the behest of Rama in search of Seetha. This sage also accords small wings and vigour to the eagle for survival until the arrival of harbinger monkeys of Rama, as this eagle has to guide the monkeys towards the location where Seetha is incarcerated."
  ],
  "closing": [
    "इति वाल्मीकि रामायणे आदि काव्ये किष्किन्ध काण्डे द्वि षष्टितमः सर्गः",
    "Thus, this is the 62nd chapter in Kishkindha Kanda of Valmiki Ramayana, the First Epic poem of India."
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "4.62.1",
      "label": "4.62.1",
      "numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "devanagari": "एवम् उक्त्वा मुनिश्रेष्ठम् अरुदम् भृश दुःखितः |\nअथ ध्यात्वा मुहूर्तम् तु भगवान् इदम् अब्रवीत्",
      "iast": "evam uktvā muniśreṣṭham arudam bhṛśa duḥkhitaḥ |\natha dhyātvā muhūrtam tu bhagavān idam abravīt",
      "translation": "\"On informing the sage in this way I wept as I was highly despaired. Then on meditating for a while that sage said this...\" Thus Sampaati continued his narration, and now he reports to Angada and others what that is said by Sage Nishaakara to him.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "evam munishreSTham uktvaa",
          "iast": "evam muniśreṣṭham uktvā",
          "devanagari": "एवं मुनिश्रेष्ठं उक्त्वा",
          "meaning": "that way, to sage the best, having said",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 0
        },
        {
          "itrans": "bhR^isha duHkhitaH arudam",
          "iast": "bhṛśa duḥkhitaḥ arudam",
          "devanagari": "भृश दुःखितः अरुदं",
          "meaning": "highly, despaired, I wept",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 3
        },
        {
          "itrans": "atha",
          "iast": "atha",
          "devanagari": "अथ",
          "meaning": "then",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 6
        },
        {
          "itrans": "bhagavaan",
          "iast": "bhagavān",
          "devanagari": "भगवान्",
          "meaning": "that godly sage",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 10
        },
        {
          "itrans": "muhuurtam dhyaatvaa idam abraviit",
          "iast": "muhūrtam dhyātvā idam abravīt",
          "devanagari": "मुहूर्तं ध्यात्वा इदं अब्रवीत्",
          "meaning": "on meditating, for a while, this, said.",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": 7
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "4.62.2",
      "label": "4.62.2",
      "numbers": [
        2
      ],
      "devanagari": "पक्षौ च ते प्रपक्षौ च पुनः अन्यौ भविष्यतः |\nचक्षुषी चैव प्राणाः च विक्रमः च बलम् च ते",
      "iast": "pakṣau ca te prapakṣau ca punaḥ anyau bhaviṣyataḥ |\ncakṣuṣī caiva prāṇāḥ ca vikramaḥ ca balam ca te",
      "translation": "\" 'Again both of your wings will emerge as small wings anew, also thus your valour, power, and life-force will comeback...' Thus Sage Nishaakara started to console Sampaati.",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "te",
          "iast": "te",
          "devanagari": "ते",
          "meaning": "to you",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 2
        },
        {
          "itrans": "punaH anyau pakSau ca",
          "iast": "punaḥ anyau pakṣau ca",
          "devanagari": "पुनः अन्यौ पक्षौ च",
          "meaning": "again, other, wings",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "pra pakSau ca",
          "iast": "pra pakṣau ca",
          "devanagari": "प्र पक्षौ च",
          "meaning": "good [small,] wings, also",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 3
        },
        {
          "itrans": "bhaviSyataH",
          "iast": "bhaviṣyataḥ",
          "devanagari": "भविष्यतः",
          "meaning": "[anew] they become [they emerge]",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 7
        },
        {
          "itrans": "te",
          "iast": "te",
          "devanagari": "ते",
          "meaning": "your",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": 16
        },
        {
          "itrans": "cakSuSii ca praaNaaH ca vikramaH ca balam ca",
          "iast": "cakṣuṣī ca prāṇāḥ ca vikramaḥ ca balam ca",
          "devanagari": "चक्षुषी च प्राणाः च विक्रमः च बलं च",
          "meaning": "eyes [sight,] also, lives' [force,] also, valour, also, power, also",
          "anvayaIndex": 5,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "[bhaviSyanti",
          "iast": "[bhaviṣyanti",
          "devanagari": "[भविष्यन्ति",
          "meaning": "will be there, they comeback.]",
          "anvayaIndex": 6,
          "verseIndex": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "4.62.3",
      "label": "4.62.3",
      "numbers": [
        3
      ],
      "devanagari": "पुराणे सुमहत् कार्यम् भविष्यम् हि मया श्रुतम् |\nदृष्टम् मे तपसा चैव श्रुत्वा च विदितम् मम",
      "iast": "purāṇe sumahat kāryam bhaviṣyam hi mayā śrutam |\ndṛṣṭam me tapasā caiva śrutvā ca viditam mama",
      "translation": "\" 'In olden days I have heard that a very great happening is going to happen indeed, and it is known to me as I perceived it ascetically...",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "su mahat kaaryam bhaviSyam hi",
          "iast": "su mahat kāryam bhaviṣyam hi",
          "devanagari": "सु महत् कार्यं भविष्यं हि",
          "meaning": "very, great, happening, will happen, indeed",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 1
        },
        {
          "itrans": "puraaNe mayaa shrutam",
          "iast": "purāṇe mayā śrutam",
          "devanagari": "पुराणे मया श्रुतं",
          "meaning": "in olden days, by me, heard",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": null
        },
        {
          "itrans": "me tapasaa caiva",
          "iast": "me tapasā caiva",
          "devanagari": "मे तपसा चैव",
          "meaning": "by me, ascetically, also thus",
          "anvayaIndex": 2,
          "verseIndex": 8
        },
        {
          "itrans": "dR^iSTam",
          "iast": "dṛṣṭam",
          "devanagari": "दृष्टं",
          "meaning": "perceived",
          "anvayaIndex": 3,
          "verseIndex": 7
        },
        {
          "itrans": "shrutvaa mama viditam",
          "iast": "śrutvā mama viditam",
          "devanagari": "श्रुत्वा मम विदितं",
          "meaning": "by hearing, to me, known.",
          "anvayaIndex": 4,
          "verseIndex": 11
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "4.62.4",
      "label": "4.62.4",
      "numbers": [
        4
      ],
      "devanagari": "राजा दशरथो नाम कश्चित् इक्ष्वाकु वर्धनः |\nतस्य पुत्रो महातेजा रामो नाम भविष्यति",
      "iast": "rājā daśaratho nāma kaścit ikṣvāku vardhanaḥ |\ntasya putro mahātejā rāmo nāma bhaviṣyati",
      "translation": "\"There is some king known as Dasharatha, an enhancer of Ikshvaku dynasty, and to him there will be a great-resplendent a son who will be known as Rama...",
      "notes": [],
      "glosses": [
        {
          "itrans": "dasharathaH naama",
          "iast": "daśarathaḥ nāma",
          "devanagari": "दशरथः नाम",
          "meaning": "Dasharatha, known as",
          "anvayaIndex": 0,
          "verseIndex": 1
        },
        {
          "itrans": "ikSvaaku vardhanaH",
          "iast": "ikṣvāku vardhanaḥ",
          "devanagari": "इक्ष्वाकु वर्धनः",
          "meaning": "Ikshvaku dynasty, enhancer of",
          "anvayaIndex": 1,
          "verseIndex": 4
